---
import ToolPage from '../../../layouts/ToolPage.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../../../data/site';

// Link to the security headers checker once it ships.
const headersTool = TOOLS.some((t) => t.slug === 'security-headers-checker');

const steps = [
  'Paste the address of your live site.',
  'We read the page, its stylesheets and its own JavaScript, and list every place it loads scripts, styles, images, fonts, data and embeds from.',
  'Remove anything you don’t recognise, choose how to handle inline scripts, and copy the policy for your host. Ship it as Report-Only first, then switch it on.',
];

const faq = [
  { q: 'What is a Content Security Policy?', a: 'A list, sent with your pages, of the places your site is allowed to load things from. If someone manages to inject a script into your page, the browser refuses to run it because it isn’t on the list. It’s the strongest protection against cross-site scripting (XSS).' },
  { q: 'Will a CSP break my site?', a: 'It can, if it misses something your site needs. That’s why the copied header starts as Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: the browser lets everything through but writes a message in the console for anything the policy would block. Click around your site for a few days, add what’s missing, then switch to Content-Security-Policy.' },
  { q: 'What are inline scripts, and why do they matter?', a: 'Code written straight into the HTML, like a script tag with code inside it, or onclick="…" on a button. A strict policy blocks it, because injected code looks the same. You can allow your exact scripts by their fingerprint (hash), allow all inline code (easier but much weaker), or move the code into .js files.' },
  { q: 'Why is there a domain I don’t recognise?', a: 'It was found in your page or code. Dashed ones were seen as addresses inside your JavaScript, which can include links your code never calls. Hover a domain to see why it’s there, and click × to remove it.' },
  { q: 'Where do I put the header?', a: 'Pick your host: a _headers file for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify, vercel.json for Vercel, or next.config.js for Next.js. The <meta> tag works anywhere, but it can’t be Report-Only and can’t stop other sites from framing yours.' },
  { q: 'Does it work for Next.js?', a: 'Yes, but Next.js writes new inline scripts on every page, so fixed hashes won’t match. Copy the prompt for your AI agent: it sets up a nonce in middleware, which is the way the Next.js docs recommend.' },
];
---
<ToolPage
  slug="csp-generator"
  title="CSP generator: build a Content Security Policy from your site · Darnly"
  description="Paste your site and get a Content Security Policy that allows exactly the scripts, styles, fonts, images and APIs it uses. Copy it for Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare, Next.js or a meta tag. Free."
  h1="CSP generator: a Content Security Policy built from your site"
  lede="Paste your site. We find every place it loads things from and build a policy that allows exactly those and blocks everything else, ready to copy for your host."
  steps={steps}
  faq={faq}
>
  <div class="csp">
    <form id="csp-form" class="ask">
      <label class="sr" for="csp-url">Website address</label>
      <input id="csp-url" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" placeholder="yoursite.com" required />
      <button id="csp-go" type="submit">Build my CSP</button>
    </form>
    <p class="error" id="csp-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

    <div id="csp-out" hidden>
      <div class="summary">
        <span class="badge" id="csp-badge"></span>
        <p class="verdict" id="csp-verdict"></p>
        <p class="sub" id="csp-sub"></p>
      </div>

      <div class="map" id="csp-map"></div>

      <div class="inline" id="csp-inline" hidden></div>

      <section class="result">
        <div class="result-h">
          <h2>Your policy</h2>
          <label class="switch">
            <input type="checkbox" id="csp-report" checked />
            <span><b>Report-Only</b> (recommended first: nothing breaks, the console shows what would be blocked)</span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div class="tabs" role="group" aria-label="Where you’ll add it">
          <button type="button" data-fmt="header" aria-pressed="true">Header</button>
          <button type="button" data-fmt="headers" aria-pressed="false">Cloudflare / Netlify</button>
          <button type="button" data-fmt="vercel" aria-pressed="false">Vercel</button>
          <button type="button" data-fmt="next" aria-pressed="false">Next.js</button>
          <button type="button" data-fmt="meta" aria-pressed="false">&lt;meta&gt; tag</button>
        </div>
        <p class="fmt-note" id="csp-fmt-note"></p>
        <pre class="code"><code id="csp-code"></code></pre>
        <div class="actions">
          <button type="button" class="act primary" id="csp-copy">Copy</button>
          <button type="button" class="act" id="csp-prompt">Copy prompt for your AI agent</button>
        </div>
        <details class="also">
          <summary>Also in the policy, for every site</summary>
          <ul>
            <li><code>default-src 'self'</code>: anything not listed above can only come from your own site.</li>
            <li><code>object-src 'none'</code>: no old plugins like Flash.</li>
            <li><code>base-uri 'self'</code>: injected code can’t change where your relative links point.</li>
            <li><code>form-action 'self'</code>: forms can only send to your site (plus any form services found).</li>
            <li><code>frame-ancestors 'self'</code>: other sites can’t show yours in a frame (stops clickjacking).</li>
            <li><code>upgrade-insecure-requests</code>: http:// files are loaded over https://. Added when you switch off Report-Only.</li>
          </ul>
        </details>
      </section>

      <details class="files" id="csp-existing" hidden>
        <summary>The policy your site sends now</summary>
        <pre class="code small"><code id="csp-existing-code"></code></pre>
      </details>
      <details class="files" id="csp-files-box" hidden>
        <summary id="csp-files-sum"></summary>
        <ul id="csp-files"></ul>
      </details>
      <p class="note" id="csp-note"></p>
      {headersTool && <p class="note">Check your other security headers with the <a href="/tools/security-headers-checker/">security headers checker</a>.</p>}
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolPage>

<script>
  import '../../../scripts/csp-generator';
</script>

<style>
  .csp [hidden] { display: none !important; }
  .csp { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  #csp-out { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); }
  .ask { display: flex; gap: 10px; }
  .ask input { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font: inherit; font-size: 18px; padding: 14px 18px; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--white); }
  .ask input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--sky); }
  .ask button { font: 600 16px/1 var(--body); padding: 0 26px; border: 0; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
  .ask button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
  .error { margin: 0; color: #B4234F; }

  .summary { border-radius: 18px; padding: 22px 24px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0B2230, #12405a); color: var(--white); display: grid; gap: 6px; }
  .badge { justify-self: start; font: 700 12px/1 var(--body); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 999px; }
  .badge.none { background: #E0A100; color: #0B2230; }
  .badge.ok { background: #1F9D55; color: var(--white); }
  .verdict { margin: 4px 0 0; font: 700 28px/1.2 var(--display); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sub { margin: 0; color: #BFD8E3; font-size: 16px; }

  .map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
  .map :global(.card) { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px; background: var(--white); display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; min-width: 0; }
  .map :global(.card-h) { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
  .map :global(.icon) { flex: none; width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 12px; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--wash); font: 700 18px/1 var(--body); color: var(--sky); }
  .map :global(h3) { margin: 0; font: 700 18px/1.2 var(--display); }
  .map :global(.dname) { font: 12px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .map :global(.what) { margin: -4px 0 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .map :global(.chips) { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .map :global(.chip) { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; max-width: 100%; padding: 4px 4px 4px 4px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--wash); border: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 13px; }
  .map :global(.chip.self) { background: #E6F6EC; border-color: #BFE5CC; padding-right: 10px; }
  .map :global(.chip.guess) { border-style: dashed; background: var(--white); }
  .map :global(.av) { flex: none; width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); font: 700 11px/1 var(--body); }
  .map :global(.chip.self .av) { background: #1F9D55; }
  .map :global(.chip.guess .av) { background: #8AA3AF; }
  .map :global(.v) { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; min-width: 0; }
  .map :global(.x) { flex: none; width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--ink-soft); cursor: pointer; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1; }
  .map :global(.x:hover) { background: #FBE3E8; color: #B4234F; }
  .map :global(.add input) { width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; font: 13px/1.2 var(--mono); padding: 7px 12px; border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 999px; background: transparent; }
  .map :global(.add input:focus) { outline: none; border-color: var(--sky); border-style: solid; }
  .map :global(.add input.bad) { border-color: #D2344F; }

  .inline { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .inline :global(.warn) { border: 1px solid #F1D48A; border-left: 6px solid #E0A100; border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px 18px; background: #FFFBEF; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  .inline :global(.warn h3) { margin: 0; font: 700 18px/1.3 var(--display); }
  .inline :global(.warn p) { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 15px; }
  .inline :global(.opts) { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .inline :global(.opt), .inline :global(.soft) { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line); cursor: pointer; }
  .inline :global(.opt:has(input:checked)) { border-color: var(--sky); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--sky); }
  .inline :global(.opt input), .inline :global(.soft input) { margin-top: 4px; }
  .inline :global(.opt span), .inline :global(.soft span) { display: grid; gap: 2px; }
  .inline :global(.opt small), .inline :global(.soft small) { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 14px; }
  .inline :global(.ex summary) { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; }
  .inline :global(.ex ul) { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; display: grid; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; }
  .inline :global(.ex code) { display: block; font: 12px/1.4 var(--mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .inline :global(.ex .hash) { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .result { border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 18px; padding: 18px 20px; background: var(--white); display: grid; gap: 12px; min-width: 0; }
  .result-h { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px 20px; align-items: center; }
  .result h2 { margin: 0; font: 700 22px/1.2 var(--display); }
  .switch { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 460px; cursor: pointer; }
  .switch input { margin-top: 3px; }
  .switch b { color: var(--ink); }
  .tabs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
  .tabs button { font: 600 14px/1 var(--body); padding: 9px 14px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; }
  .tabs button[aria-pressed='true'] { background: var(--ink); color: var(--white); border-color: var(--ink); }
  .fmt-note { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .code { margin: 0; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 12px; background: #0B2230; color: #E6F4FA; font: 13px/1.55 var(--mono); white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; max-height: 360px; overflow: auto; }
  .code.small { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 12px; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .act { font: 600 15px/1 var(--body); padding: 11px 18px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--white); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; }
  .act.primary { background: var(--sky); color: var(--white); border-color: var(--sky); }
  .also summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; }
  .also ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 6px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .also code { font: 12px var(--mono); color: var(--ink); }

  .files { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; padding: 12px 18px; background: var(--white); }
  .files summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .files ul { margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 4px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .files :global(li) { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .note { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .ask { flex-direction: column; }
    .ask button { padding: 14px 26px; }
    .verdict { font-size: 22px; }
  }
</style>
